Thanks. I've planned these as TAS-80, waiting for your acknowledgement:
- property names aligned to the top, with values top-aligned by default;
- 'livtk's own for the stage' renamed to 'Default';
- the run (its status and Start/Stop, as it looks now) moved into the panel's title bar, right after the task's key.

Build 232. The new icons are on the run's actions:
- play leads Start, in the panel's title bar;
- stop leads Stop there, and 'Stop them all' in the quit dialog;
- fast-forward leads 'Continue them' in the dialog that offers back runs a quit stopped;
- block marks a blocked task's 'Waits for …' status.
One icon for one meaning: the Blocked tag in the rows now uses the same block icon instead of the brick. Say if you'd rather keep the brick there. The other new icons stay in the folder unused. App tests pass (274). scripts/check's 10k timing test failed again, while the TAS-83 run was compiling alongside; it's the same machine-load failure as before.

Done. No doc or skill told anyone to keep a terminal watching for acks; that was already true. What was missing was the skills' half.
- The work skill has a new section, 'When livtk started you (a run)'. It says:
  - your last words in a turn become a note on the task;
  - to ask a question, end your turn with it;
  - when you need a command you may not be allowed, run it: livtk puts it to the human with Allow and Deny. Never ask for permission in words; a note can't grant it.
  - in a worktree, commit everything on your branch;
  - before review, run the checks and commit.
  These are the lessons from the TAS-85 run.
- The work skill now commits before review (step 6). Done then commits the record only (step 7).
- README: the app is where you follow runs. scripts/watch stays for setups with no app (an agent in a terminal), and it says so. I kept it rather than removing it: sessions like this one still use it.

I still couldn't check the library, so the plan is unchanged. Your allow list didn't cover it: this session can only read files inside `/Users/karlwerk/Workspace/tasks`, and the library source is in `~/.cargo/registry`, outside that folder.

