TAS-104 is written but not verified: this session couldn't run cargo or `scripts/check`, so nothing has been compiled or tested. I haven't committed it and haven't moved it to review. It stays in **doing**.

**What the change does**
- **New file `model/listing.rs`:** one description of what a list of each kind offers (a "new" button, a board, priority, grouping by project, nesting, and what to call one item). You look it up with `View::listing_spec()`. The `View::Tasks` checks in the dock and palette now read from it; the grep finds none left in `dock.rs` or `palette.rs`.
- **Dock:** Projects now has the New project button. Lessons, Decisions and Findings get none. "Nest sub-projects" / "Nest sub-tasks" shows only where the kind nests. Priority ordering is hidden where the kind has no priority.
- **Empty text:** it reads "…or P for a new project" in Projects. Views where nothing can be made leave out the "new" part. The list and the board build the text the same way.
- **Projects board:** columns are Active, Proposed, Paused, Done. Cards use the project's own state menu, have no priority button, and show progress and health. A drop on a column moves the project there.
- **No priority for projects:** grouping, ordering and filtering by priority are gone in Projects, and so is grouping by project. The model also refuses them if the palette or a saved view asks.
- **Two changes the plan didn't name:**
  - Projects now default to "last updated" order instead of priority, and older saved views fall back to it.
  - A declared kind's board was being drawn as a plain list; it now draws as a board.
- I removed `Making::for_view` and `Making::lists`, since the new description replaces them.

**Files:** `model/listing.rs` (new), `model.rs`, `model/making.rs`, `model/palette.rs`, `model/saved.rs`, `ui/dock.rs`, `ui/list.rs`, `ui/mod.rs`, `tests/app/projects.rs` (5 new tests), `tests/app/ui.rs` (2 new tests). The notes are on TAS-104.

**What I need from you:** run `scripts/check` (or `cargo test -p livtk-app`), or allow cargo in this run. Once it passes I'll fix anything it turns up, run `cargo fmt`, commit, and move the task to review.

