The new layering for Activity is written but untested. This session can't run `cargo test` or `scripts/check`: both need approval, and there's nobody here to give it. So the code has never been compiled, and I haven't committed it or moved the task to review. It's still in doing.

**Files changed:**
- `crates/livtk-app/src/model/timeline.rs`: `stints_of` replaces `session_of`. Two new lookups, `Mark::on_rail` (creation and session bookkeeping) and `Mark::resets` (state moves), keep the rules in one place.
  - A lane is now one stint: either a run from Started to Ended, or an interactive agent (its actor plus its conversation, so `claude:refuter` gets its own lane).
  - An agent's own move is the last mark on its lane. If it has no lane open, the move goes on the rail.
  - Every move closes the lanes open before it, except a run that's still going.
  - Claude's events with no session get a lane instead of the rail.
  - Lane allocation, folding and the drawing code (`ui/timeline/`) are unchanged.
- `crates/livtk-app/tests/app/timeline.rs`: 7 new model tests, one per rule in the acceptance check, plus helpers to build creation events, moves inside a conversation, and `claude:agent` actors.
- `docs/design.md`: the Timeline entry now states the two levels, when a lane opens and closes, and that lanes never nest.

**How I checked it:** only by reading. I traced the 7 new tests and the 4 existing timeline tests through the code by hand, plus the two Activity UI tests in `ui.rs`. Their setups get the same lanes as before; in the sticky-header test the lane still starts at row 2. I also rewrote one closure as a plain loop because I wasn't sure it would compile. My notes are on TAS-105.

**Not done:**
- `cargo test -p livtk-app --test app timeline` and `scripts/check` were never run.
- I haven't checked TAS-98 and TAS-92 in the running app.
- No commit, and no move to review.

